    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Bank transaction categoriser (AI) for a sheet\nPaste your bank export into a sheet and the AI adds a category for each row, so tax time is easier. Always review the results.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b897bfb1-5f47-5cc1-a99d-477bac3110b8",
      "name": "Note: what this does",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup (about 10 minutes)\n1. Use a Google Sheet with a tab named **Transactions** and these headers in row 1 (see `sheet-headers.csv`).\n2. Fill the input columns (description). Leave category, reason empty: the AI fills it.\n3. Open **Settings**: sheet URL and how many rows to process per run.\n4. Connect Google Sheets and OpenAI on the nodes with warnings.\n5. Run once by hand, check the results, then switch to **Active**. It only touches rows where category is empty.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "b0fbc4be-525a-5bc8-b39a-6352d15248c9",
      "name": "Note: setup",
